  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1201 AM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nDeeper moisture will spread across our CWA Sunday. As the upper \ntrough moves across we can expect better rain chances. Models have \ncontinued to show only moderate rainfall totals with no significant \nimpacts. The last rain chances will exit our eastern counties Sunday \nevening. An upper level ridge will move in starting Monday bringing \ndry weather back that will continue until mid-day Wednesday. \nMoisture will surge from the Gulf bringing low chances for rain \nWednesday night and Thursday.\n\nWe don't expect any big temperature changes Sunday. After the rain \nmoves away Monday winds will become northeasterly bringing in \ncooler, drier air. Models are showing cooler temperatures for Monday \nand Tuesday than they have the last few days. With low level flow \nbecoming easterly to southeasterly warmer air will return for \nWednesday and Thursday.",
